      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/2014_at_Sea_Lawn_Terrace_16.JPG",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2014_at_Sea_Lawn_Terrace_16.JPG",
      "width": 1366,
      "height": 910,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0",
      "artist": "Geof Sheppard",
      "description": "When the sea wall north of Dawlish station was reopened in April 2014 there was still work to be done to finish the job. This view, taken eight days after train services resumed, shows a distinct dip in track level where the new wall has been constructed. A temporary speed restriction of 30 mph is in place through here, easing to 60 (35 for trains with heavier suspensions) just beyond the dip.",
      "dateCreated": "2014-04-12",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "south-devon-railway-sea-wall-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gbvx",
